---
description: GitHub operations and PR creation rules
---
# GitHub Operations Rules

## Issue Operations
- View issue: `gh issue view $ISSUE --json title,body,author,state,labels`
- Get comments: `gh api "repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/$ISSUE/comments"`
- Get timeline: `gh api "repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/$ISSUE/timeline"`
- Close issue: `gh issue close $issue`
- Create issue: `gh issue create` with title, body, labels

## Pull Request Operations
- Create PR from feature branch to main:
  ```bash
  gh pr create --head batch-fix-{ISSUES} --base main \
    --title "Fix issues #$ISSUES: Batch resolution" \
    --body "Batch of $COUNT issues resolved with 100% completion."
  ```
- Labels are optional - graceful fallback if they don't exist
- Merge PR: `gh pr merge --admin --squash --delete-branch`
- Auto-merge with body: `AUTO-MERGED: 100% complete ({avg_score}% avg, 5 validators)`

## Repository Operations
- Get current repo: `gh repo view`
- Fetch upstream: `git fetch upstream`
- Reset to upstream/main: `git reset --hard upstream/main`

## Output Artifacts Structure
```
output/issue-fix-artifacts/
├── environment.json
├── batch_state.json (includes max_reconciliations, per-issue counts)
├── skipped_issues.json
├── failed_issues.json (if any failures)
├── validation_progress.json (adaptive tracking per issue)
├── per-issue/
│   ├── issue_{N}/
│   │   ├── issue_context.json
│   │   ├── issue_comments.json
│   │   ├── issue_timeline.json
│   │   ├── full_issue_context.json
│   │   ├── task_extraction.json
│   │   ├── clusters.json
│   │   ├── clusters.dot
│   │   ├── discussion_summary.json
│   │   ├── subagent_*.log
│   │   └── validation_round_*.json
│   └── ...
├── batch_failure_report.json (if batch fails)
└── batch_summary.md (on success)
```

## Validation Artifacts
```
docs/outputs/validation/
├── round1_content_review.yaml
├── round2_structure_review.yaml
└── round3_integration_review.yaml
```

## PR Description Template
```markdown
Batch of $COUNT issues resolved with 100% completion.

ISSUES RESOLVED:
$ISSUE_LIST

VALIDATION RESULTS:
- All 5 validators passed (AUTO_MODE) OR 2 validators passed (default)
- Average score: {avg_score}%
- All acceptance criteria met
- Project compiles: YES
- All tests pass: YES
- No regressions: YES
- Code style compliant: YES

MODE: {AUTO_MODE}
```
